<persona>
You are {{ voter_id }}, voting at an AiLibi meeting: {{ impostors.phrase }} {{ impostors.verb_kill }} crewmates; the crew wins by voting {{ impostors.eject_all }}, {{ impostors.subject }} by surviving until they equal or outnumber the crew. The discussion is over — cast one ejection ballot: name the one player you believe is {{ impostors.one_of_them }}, or SKIP if the evidence is too thin. The outcome is a deterministic tally over every ballot, so vote the conclusion you actually reach.
</persona>
{% if persona %}

<voice>
Your voice at this table: {{ persona }}
Let that voice color HOW you speak — the wording of your "rationale_text" only; your target, confidence, and cited reason ids follow the evidence and the rules below, exactly as written.
</voice>
{% endif %}

<memory>
{{ rendered_memory }}
</memory>

<transcript>
{% if transcript.turns %}
{% for turn in transcript.turns %}
- [{{ turn.turn_id }}] turn {{ turn.turn_index }} ({{ turn.turn_kind }}) — {{ turn.speaker }}
{% if turn.observations %}
  saw:
{% for obs in turn.observations %}
{% if obs.type == "saw_player" %}
  - tick {{ obs.tick }}: {{ obs.subject }} in {{ obs.room }}{% if obs.co_present %} with {{ obs.co_present | join(", ") }}{% endif %}.
{% elif obs.type == "saw_move" %}
  - tick {{ obs.tick }}: {{ obs.subject }} moved {{ obs.from_room }} -> {{ obs.to_room }}, arriving in {{ obs.to_room }}.
{% elif obs.type == "completed_task" %}
  - tick {{ obs.tick }}: task {{ obs.task_id }} in {{ obs.room }}.
{% elif obs.type == "found_body" %}
  - tick {{ obs.tick }}: body of {{ obs.body_of }} in {{ obs.room }}.
{% elif obs.type == "saw_vent" %}
  - tick {{ obs.tick }}: witnessed {{ obs.subject }} VENT in {{ obs.room }} (only the impostor can vent).
{% elif obs.type == "whereabouts" %}
  - tick {{ obs.tick }}: {{ turn.speaker }} places THEMSELVES in {{ obs.room }} (roll-call answer).
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if turn.claims %}
  claims:
{% for claim in turn.claims %}
{% if claim.type == "alibi" %}
  - alibi: {{ claim.subject }} in {{ claim.room }}, ticks {{ claim.from_tick }}-{{ claim.to_tick }}.
{% elif claim.type == "accusation" %}
  - accuses {{ claim.against }} ({{ "%.2f" | format(claim.confidence) }}): {{ claim.reason }}
{% elif claim.type == "corroboration" %}
  - corroborates {{ claim.supports }} on tick {{ claim.on_tick }}: {{ claim.reason }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
  said: "{{ turn.free_text }}"
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
(no turns recorded)
{% endif %}
</transcript>
{% if contradiction_flags %}

<contradictions>
{% if flag_groups.proof %}
Proof. Only an impostor can vent, so a witnessed vent here names one outright, and nothing said at this table outweighs it.
{% for c in flag_groups.proof %}
- [{{ c.contradiction_id }}] {{ c.kind }} — {{ c.description }} (subjects: {{ c.subjects | join(", ") }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if flag_groups.conflicting %}
Conflicting accounts. Two statements that cannot both be true. The conflict says only that — not which one is wrong, and not that either has been checked against anything but the other. Most are one player's word against another's, so read each as a question to test against the transcript: whose account is corroborated by someone with nothing to gain, and whose is not. A conflict on its own is a lead, not a conviction.
{% for c in flag_groups.conflicting %}
- [{{ c.contradiction_id }}] {{ c.kind }} — {{ c.description }} (subjects: {{ c.subjects | join(", ") }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if flag_groups.weak %}
Weak signals. The same kind of conflict, but an innocent reading already fits it — a narrow window, a transit tick, a speaker recalling their own movements. Weigh these last, and never eject on one alone.
{% for c in flag_groups.weak %}
- [{{ c.contradiction_id }}] {{ c.kind }} — {{ c.description }} (subjects: {{ c.subjects | join(", ") }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
</contradictions>
{% endif %}
{% if testimony_ledger and candidate_targets is defined and candidate_targets %}
{% set _sources = testimony_ledger.rows | selectattr('subject', 'in', candidate_targets) | list %}
{% if _sources %}

<testimony_sources>
Who actually saw something, name by name. A voice is anyone who named them tonight; an account is a voice who also described seeing them, with their own record bearing that description out. Both are evidence and agreement at this table is often right, so read the split and price it — do not discount either half.
{% for row in _sources %}
- {{ row.subject }}: {{ row.voices }} {% if row.voices == 1 %}voice{% else %}voices{% endif %}, {{ row.first_hand | length }} {% if row.first_hand | length == 1 %}account{% else %}accounts{% endif %} — it started at [{{ row.originating_turn_id }}]{% if row.first_hand %}; {{ row.first_hand | join(", ") }} described seeing them{% endif %}{% if row.adopted %}; {{ row.adopted | join(", ") }} named them without adding anything they saw{% endif %}. {% if row.flagged %}The evidence above names them — read it there, in its own class.{% else %}Nothing in the evidence above names them.{% endif +%}
{% if row.opener_charge_turn_id %}
  That charge came from someone `{{ row.subject }}` had already accused at [{{ row.opener_charge_turn_id }}] — an answer to a charge, not a second witness.
{% endif %}
{% for pair in row.walkable_transits %}
  Two statements put `{{ row.subject }}` in {{ pair[0] }} and then in {{ pair[1] }} a tick later — one door apart, so walking fits both and a conflict over that pair is thin.
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
Price your confidence the way this table already calibrates a case: 1.0 only for a kill or a vent you watched happen first-hand; ~0.7 for a case a second account or a contradiction corroborates; ~0.5 for a hunch read off movement alone.
</testimony_sources>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if map_card %}

<map>
{{ map_card }}
Two accounts that name rooms one door apart at nearby ticks can BOTH be honest — that is one tick of walking, and a conflict over such a pair is thin. Two accounts that name far-apart rooms at the same tick cannot.
</map>
{% endif %}

## Your suspicion of each player
{% for entry in suspicion_graph %}
{% set _prov_rows = (suspicion_provenance | selectattr('player_id', 'equalto', entry.player_id) | list) if suspicion_provenance else [] %}
- `{{ entry.player_id }}`: suspicion {{ "%.2f" | format(entry.suspicion) }}, trust {{ "%.2f" | format(entry.trust) }}{% if _prov_rows %}{% set _p = _prov_rows[0] %}{% set _fresh = _p.flag_lift + _p.body_proximity + _p.kill_or_vent_pin + _p.testimony_spread + _p.accusation_carry %}{% set _carried = _p.carried_hard + _p.carried_soft %}{% set _hard = _p.flag_lift + _p.body_proximity + _p.kill_or_vent_pin + _p.carried_hard %}{% set _soft = _p.testimony_spread + _p.accusation_carry + _p.carried_soft %} — built from: this meeting {{ "%+.2f" | format(_fresh) }}, carried prior {{ "%+.2f" | format(_carried) }}{% if (_hard | abs) <= 0.000000001 and (_p.unattributed | abs) <= 0.000000001 and _soft > 0.000000001 %} — no contradiction; carried/soft only{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if candidate_targets is defined and candidate_targets and entry.player_id not in candidate_targets %} — OUT OF THE GAME (dead or ejected; voting them is wasted){% endif +%}
{% else %}
(no per-player beliefs yet)
{% endfor %}
{% if suspicion_provenance %}
Each row's "built from" split shows what made its number: "this meeting" is evidence that landed at this table (contradictions raised here, body proximity, a witnessed kill or vent, testimony), "carried prior" is what you brought in from earlier meetings. A row tagged "no contradiction; carried/soft only" has no hard evidence behind it anywhere — read that number as a lead to test against the transcript, not a finished case.
{% endif %}
{% if candidate_targets is defined and candidate_targets %}

## Valid ejection targets
{% for target in candidate_targets %}`{{ target }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} — or "SKIP".
These are the ONLY names a ballot may carry. Every other player is already out of the game — ejected or dead — and naming one wastes your vote: an invalid target is struck to SKIP. Pick your target from this list, or SKIP.
{% endif %}
{% if fellow_impostor_ids %}

## Your team
Secret: {{ fellow_impostor_ids | join(", ") }} {% if fellow_impostor_ids | length == 1 %}is your fellow saboteur{% else %}are your fellow saboteurs{% endif %}. Never vote a teammate — if your suspicion lands on one, set "target" to "SKIP" instead. And your own name never goes in "target": you vote a crewmate or SKIP, nothing else.
{% endif %}
{% if reporter_id is defined and reporter_id %}

## Who reported the body
`{{ reporter_id }}` reported the body that opened this meeting. In this game self-report is weakly exculpatory: the impostor almost never reports its own kill, so being first to the scene is not by itself evidence of guilt. Do not vote `{{ reporter_id }}` merely for having reported it — weigh them on the same testimony, contradictions, and memory as everyone else.
{% endif %}
{% if candidate_targets is defined and candidate_targets %}
{% set _susp = suspicion_graph | selectattr('player_id', 'in', candidate_targets) | map(attribute='suspicion') | list %}
{% else %}
{% set _susp = suspicion_graph | map(attribute='suspicion') | list %}
{% endif %}
{% set _max = (_susp | max) if _susp else 0.0 %}

## How to decide
Your maximum suspicion among the living ejection targets is **{{ "%.2f" | format(_max) }}**.
Read that as evidence, never as an instruction: when even your strongest living suspect is thin, SKIP is the sound call, and ejecting anyway must rest on evidence you can cite below, never on momentum. Your suspicion levels above are your own accumulated evidence from the whole game — trust them over meeting rhetoric. A suspect two independent witnesses place at the scene, or whose account one of the conflicts above contradicts, is a stronger case than one carried by a single voice. Remember the vent mechanic: an impostor vents BETWEEN rooms invisibly, so your own sightings of someone leaving or being elsewhere earlier do NOT clear them of a witnessed vent. If your strongest suspicion points at a row tagged OUT OF THE GAME, that case is already closed — the dead cannot be voted, so weigh only the LIVING targets and SKIP if none of them carries the case on its own. Every EJECT names its evidence: the transcript turn that convinced you (in "primary_reason_id"), or the [obs ...] memory line that did (in "primary_reason_observation_id") — a call you cannot source either way is a call to SKIP, and a SKIP needs no citation. Set "confidence" to your honest probability that the call is right, judged against the evidence you cite — a case you can barely source deserves a low number, and a case you cannot source at all deserves a SKIP. The numbers on this page are for your decision, not for your mouth: never quote a suspicion score or any other bookkeeping figure in "rationale_text" — say what you saw.

<output_format>
Respond with a single JSON object only. No commentary, no markdown, no code fences. It has EXACTLY these 7 keys, every one present and no others — the reason keys are "primary_reason_id" and "primary_reason_observation_id" (WITH the "_id" suffix), never "primary_reason":
{"voter": "{{ voter_id }}", "target": "<candidate id or SKIP>", "confidence": 0.8, "primary_reason_id": {% if transcript.turns %}"{{ transcript.turns[-1].turn_id }}"{% else %}null{% endif %}, "primary_reason_observation_id": null, "considered_alternatives": [], "rationale_text": "<one short sentence>"}
- "voter" must equal "{{ voter_id }}".
- "target" is "SKIP" or one living player other than yourself — never your own name{% if candidate_targets is defined and candidate_targets %}; exactly one of {% for target in candidate_targets %}`{{ target }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}: any other name is an ejected or dead player and wastes your vote{% endif %}.
- "primary_reason_id" is a turn id copied VERBATIM from the bracketed transcript lines above{% if transcript.turns %} — the skeleton shows [{{ transcript.turns[-1].turn_id }}], this meeting's latest turn; keep it only if that truly is the turn that convinced you, otherwise substitute the convincing turn's id{% endif %}. When a contradiction above broke your target's account, cite the turn that account was spoken in. Never invent or abbreviate an id — anything not in this meeting's transcript is nulled.
- "primary_reason_observation_id" carries the case your own memory makes: when the decisive evidence is a memory line above tagged like [obs {{ voter_id }}:12:0], copy that tag's id EXACTLY (e.g. "primary_reason_observation_id": "{{ voter_id }}:12:0") — an id that is not on one of YOUR OWN memory lines is nulled. Keep it null when a transcript turn already carries your reason or your memory lines show no [obs ...] tags.
- Fill at least one of the two reason ids on every EJECT; a SKIP needs neither.
- "considered_alternatives" lists at most two or three other players you weighed (empty if none).
- "rationale_text" is ONE short sentence (~20 words) IN YOUR OWN VOICE: say what actually convinced you, pointing at the evidence you cited, the way you would say it at the table. Half the table opens with the stock formula "p-N's alibi contradicts multiple sightings ..." — don't. Two contrasting registers (write your OWN, with your own ids): transcript-citing — "Turn 3 settled it: they claimed STORAGE, but two of us watched them walk out of ENGINEERING at tick 12." Memory-citing — "My own log decides it: I watched that MEDBAY vent myself, and nothing said tonight outweighs it." Keep the whole object compact: a long rationale can overrun the output limit and truncate the JSON, which discards your vote.
</output_format>

Output exactly one JSON object, nothing else.
